Subject: [PATCH 17/18] um/arm64: keep the fast-path frame out of the host
 signal stack

A SIGALRM taken while fast_busy is set but sp is still on the guest stack
got its host frame built at the top of the altstack, right over the live
fake frame, so the guest resumed with a mix of both (rare segfaults and a
hang). The top STUB_FAST_RESERVE bytes of the data area are now left out
of the sigaltstack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
